// Terms the documentation explores, stated as identities so that `rewrite` can
// address them.
//
// `rewrite` works a *goal* — two terms and the claim that they are equal — and
// has no way to name a bare sentence, because everything it does is about a
// goal. A term worth looking at is therefore a term worth stating an identity
// over, and the cheapest such identity is a reflexive one.
//
// What that buys is not nothing. `rewrite tests pair_check -t <tactic>` runs the
// tactic on the left and leaves the right as written, so the side-by-side is the
// listing *and* a diff against where it started. Under a tactic that closes the
// goal, what gets printed is the term the two sides met at — which for
// `-t unfold_all` is the flat sentence, one call opened all the way down.
//
// These claim nothing, and are not meant to: they are addresses. Real claims
// live in `identities.hana`, whose narrative is the laws and not the tooling.

// The type checker generates a `check` sentence for every type, and an enum
// variant's is a deep tree of branches over tags — which is why the tactic
// documentation reaches for these two rather than for anything hand-written.
identity pair_check
    { jump super::type_tests::RelEnum::Pair::check }
  = { jump super::type_tests::RelEnum::Pair::check };

identity state_check
    { jump super::queue::State::check }
  = { jump super::queue::State::check };

// The term `lifting` is written for: a precondition, a computation and a
// postcondition, all of it buried in branch arms that test the same four
// symbols over and over. `barista.hana` states the claim that it is constantly
// `true`; this one claims nothing and is only the address the tactic
// documentation reaches for.
identity emit_pre_and_post
    { jump super::barista::customer_impl::emit_does_pre_and_post }
  = { jump super::barista::customer_impl::emit_does_pre_and_post };

// The same shape as `emit_pre_and_post`, with two symbols where that has four
// states and a pair where it has an event enum — small enough to read a whole
// derivation off. `types_test.hana` says what still blocks the claim.
identity number_pre_and_post
    { jump super::types_test::number_does_pre_and_post }
  = { jump super::types_test::number_does_pre_and_post };
